  "interpretation": "2.6 A TRANSFERS. The best-F1 cutoff is 2.5-2.7 A for every metal and F1@2.6 is within 0.004 of each metal's own best (Ir 0.9284 vs 0.9322 at 2.7; Rh 0.9381 vs 0.9457 at 2.5). The element filter was the real gap: the pre-A94 set reached 35-56% of true bonds; +halides 46-71%; +carbon/organic 100% for all six. Carbon alone is 295-721 bonds per metal (28-51%). Adding C therefore moves the rule from 'misses half the coordination sphere' to 'covers it', at a measured precision of 0.88-0.95 (the false positives are non-bonded metal-C contacts under 2.6 A).",
  "verdict": "2.6 A VALID FOR ALL SIX METALS; CARBON ADDED TO THE CANDIDATE SET",
  "generated": "2026-10-19"
}
